AbiWord @VERSION@ - the word processor (GTK 3) for RISC OS

AbiWord 3.0.8 by the AbiWord developers (GPL version 2 or later), on GTK
3 through riscos-gtk's RISC OS backend: styles, tables, headers and
footers, footnotes, lists, pictures and page layout, with OpenDocument
(.odt), Word (.doc, .docx), RTF, HTML, plain text and AbiWord's own .abw
files.

This is a first test build: not everything has been tried on RISC OS yet,
so please report what goes wrong (see riscos-gtk's release notes).

Using it
- Run it: AbiWord opens a new document and puts its icon on the icon bar.
  Or drop a document on !AbiWord in a Filer window.
- The icon bar icon: Select brings AbiWord's window to the front; Menu
  gives Info, Choices... (AbiWord's Preferences) and Quit.
- Files dropped on the icon bar icon, or Word files double-clicked in the
  Filer while AbiWord is loaded, open in a window of their own (or in the
  new, empty document if nothing has been typed in it).
- Click Menu over a window for AbiWord's menus.
- File > Save As: a RISC OS Save box (the format is chosen from the name,
  e.g. .odt, .docx, .rtf, .abw); File > Open: an Open box.
- AbiWord's settings are kept in <Choices$Write>.AbiWord.
- Left Alt and a menu's underlined letter opens that menu (Alt+F: File),
  at the window's top left; F10 opens the whole menu there.
- Spelling: British English, with the dictionary AbiWord carries. For
  other languages, put hunspell dictionaries (e.g. de_DE/dic and
  de_DE/aff, from LibreOffice's or your Linux distribution's) in
  <Choices$Write>.GTK.Dictionaries: every GTK program that checks
  spelling uses them. Words you add are kept in <Choices$Write>.GTK.Enchant.

Not in this build: grammar checking, the thesaurus,
collaboration, equations (MathML), WordPerfect and Works files, PDF
import, SVG pictures, help.

Messages
AbiWord's messages go to <Wimp$ScrapDir>.AbiWord.Log.

Needs
RISC OS 5 on an ARMv7 or later machine (Raspberry Pi 2 or later, ARMX6,
Titanium...), SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later, ARMEABISupport and Iconv
(PackMan). PThreadTicker is included.
Fonts: AbiWord uses the desktop's own fonts (Homerton, Trinity, Corpus,
and any in !Fonts), as the desktop draws them. The first time it starts
it makes copies they can be used from, in <Choices$Write>.GTK.FontCache
(about a second; again only when a font changes). It also carries DejaVu
Sans, and with FontConfig and fonts from PackMan installed it uses those
too, as other FontConfig programs do. The Log's "fonts:" lines say which
fonts it found.

